    {
      "id": "cad7b0b42ede0b0577ea151d",
      "name": "Nexaris Scientific (Contact Angle Meter)",
      "categoryId": "a2588b40ca23f8e1f166a050",
      "sku": "",
      "overview": "An optical surface characterization system for contact angle, wettability, surface free energy and interfacial analysis, with high-resolution imaging and automated measurement capabilities.",
      "description": "The Nexaris Scientific Contact Angle Meter is an advanced surface characterization system engineered for precise evaluation of contact angle, wettability, surface free energy, and interfacial properties. The system utilizes sessile-drop optical analysis with high-resolution imaging and automated measurement capabilities for accurate and reproducible surface characterization.\n\nIt supports static and dynamic contact angle measurements, including advancing, receding, sliding, and roll-off angle analysis. The automated liquid dispensing system ensures consistent droplet formation, while the motorized sample stage provides precise specimen positioning during measurements.\n\nAdvanced image-processing algorithms enable automatic droplet detection, edge identification, profile fitting, and contact angle calculation. The system can also support surface free-energy calculations using established analytical models such as Owens-Wendt, Fowkes, Wu, Zisman, and OWRK.\n\nThe Nexaris Scientific Contact Angle Meter is suitable for evaluating coatings, polymers, films, glass, metals, ceramics, composites, textiles, membranes, electronic materials, paints, adhesives, and advanced engineered surfaces.\n\nDesigned for research, quality control, and industrial applications, the system provides a reliable solution for surface treatment evaluation, adhesion studies, coating development, material characterization, and wettability analysis.",
      "catalogueUrl": "",
      "imageUrl": "/uploads/nexaris-contact-angle-meter.png",
      "images": [
        "/uploads/nexaris-contact-angle-meter.png"
      ],
      "features": [
        "Static and dynamic contact angle measurements, including advancing, receding, sliding, and roll-off angles.",
        "Automated liquid dispensing for consistent droplet formation and a motorized sample stage for precise positioning.",
        "High-resolution imaging with automatic droplet detection, edge identification, profile fitting, and angle calculation.",
        "Surface free-energy calculations using models such as Owens-Wendt, Fowkes, Wu, Zisman, and OWRK.",
        "Suitable for surface treatment evaluation, adhesion studies, coating development, and wettability analysis."
      ],
